Explanation of the change:

1. We detect `url("…")` and `url('…')` first, delegating the entire quoted region to the standard string modes (which correctly match nested `)` inside the quotes).
2. If neither quoted form matches, we fall back to your original unquoted‐URL rule.  

This ensures that parentheses inside quoted URLs (e.g. `background (01).jpg`) no longer prematurely close the highlight block.
